spans.s:
guṇa,
(1) m. (Skt. and Pali id., not recorded in this use), advantage: Mv 〔i.155.7〕 (vs) kaṃ vā guṇaṃ karoti, or what good does it do? what use is it?;
(2) m. (= Pali guṇa), cluster, bouquet, garland: LV 〔214.19〕 (vs) sugandhamālāṃ guṇapuṣpasaṃcayāṃ (acc. pl.), bunches of flowers in clusters, of garlanded flowers; kaṇṭhe-guṇa, see this; mālā-guṇa-parikṣiptaḥ Mvy 〔9463〕. See also antraguṇa (in which guṇa may perhaps mean lit. garland, chain, i.e. of the intestines).

Guṇamati,
(1) n. of a Bodhisattva: LV 〔292.20〕;
(2) n. of a teacher: Mvy 〔3488〕.
